## Frozen workloads

Natural replay uses the same structural selection frozen for P1/P2: 10 cones from adder, cavlc, int2float, priority, and router. `bar` was scanned but had zero cones satisfying the frozen 9-12-support / <=128-source-node admission rule and is therefore not a timed circuit.

Gate-P is the exact 36-case N1/P1/P2 generator family (depths 6, 8, 10; 12 cases per depth). Before timing, all 36 P3-run direct digests and frozen structural-work fields are checked against the frozen P2 reference.

## Basic reproduction

Run from the bundle root so the sibling import directories are present.

```bash
python cm_n2_p3_run/n2_p3_harness.py --mode selection --out cm_n2_p3_run/repro_selection.json
python cm_n2_p3_run/n2_p3_harness.py --mode fuzz --out cm_n2_p3_run/repro_fuzz.json
python cm_n2_p3_run/n2_p3_harness.py --mode gatep --out cm_n2_p3_run/repro_gatep.json
python cm_n2_p3_run/n2_p3_harness.py --mode natural-case --case-id 'adder:f[4]' --out cm_n2_p3_run/repro_adder_f4.json
```

Repeat the natural-case command for the 10 case IDs listed in `natural_selection_frozen.json`.

The original environment imposed a short per-command wall timeout. The long `cavlc:35` timing schedule was therefore split into deterministic schedule-index ranges with `run_p3_nat_chunk.py`. This does **not** change the arm order, random seed, repetition IDs, frozen algorithm, or timing endpoint. Example:

```bash
python cm_n2_p3_run/run_p3_nat_chunk.py --case-id 'cavlc:35' --symbolic --start 0 --end 0 --out cm_n2_p3_run/repro_cavlc35_symbolic.json
python cm_n2_p3_run/run_p3_nat_chunk.py --case-id 'cavlc:35' --start 0 --end 15 --out cm_n2_p3_run/repro_cavlc35_t0_15.json
```

Continue with ranges 15-30, 30-45, 45-60, and 60-75. There are 25 repetitions of each of the three primary arms, randomized into one frozen 75-entry schedule.

## Independent verification

After the bundled merged results are present:

```bash
python cm_n2_p3_run/independent_verify.py
```

The verifier does not import the experiment harness to recalculate its primary ratios. It checks preregistration/harness hashes, Git blob identities for all six EPFL files, exact natural case IDs, row counts and schedules, all correctness flags, 1,000-case fuzz status, P3 accepted-fold utilization, direct Gate-P identity against the frozen P2 reference, natural structural identity when P3 abstains, and recalculates the main paired-median geometric-mean ratios.

Expected verification status: `PASS`.

